lesson.body:
**Companies**: companies covered by the Ind AS roadmap (listed companies, unlisted companies with net worth of ₹250 crore or more, their holding, subsidiary, JV and associate companies, and specified NBFCs, banks and insurers as notified) follow Ind AS. All other companies follow AS under the Companies (AS) Rules, 2021.

A **Small and Medium-sized Company (SMC)** gets some exemptions and relaxations (for example AS 17 does not apply, AS 20 diluted EPS is not required). A company is an SMC if it:

- is not listed and not in the process of listing (equity or debt) in India or abroad;
- is not a bank, financial institution or insurance company;
- had turnover (excluding other income) not exceeding **₹250 crore** in the immediately preceding accounting year;
- had borrowings (including public deposits) not exceeding **₹50 crore** at any time during the immediately preceding accounting year; and
- is not a holding or subsidiary of a company that is not an SMC.

**Non-company entities** (firms, LLPs, trusts carrying on business) follow ICAI's AS, classified by ICAI announcement into a large category that applies all AS in full and MSME categories with exemptions. ICAI revised this classification in recent years, so check the current ICAI announcement before applying exact thresholds.

questions.answer:
An intangible asset from development is recognised only if the enterprise can demonstrate all of the following:

- technical feasibility of completing the asset so it will be available for use or sale;
- its intention to complete the asset and use or sell it;
- its ability to use or sell the asset;
- how the asset will generate probable future economic benefits, for example a market for the output or the asset, or its usefulness if used internally;
- availability of adequate technical, financial and other resources to complete development and use or sell the asset;
- its ability to measure reliably the expenditure attributable to the asset during development.

Expenditure before these criteria are met is expensed and cannot be reinstated later. If the research and development phases cannot be separated, all expenditure is treated as research.

A liability is classified as current when it satisfies any of these criteria:

- it is expected to be settled in the company's normal operating cycle;
- it is held primarily for the purpose of being traded;
- it is due to be settled within twelve months after the reporting date; or
- the company does not have an unconditional right to defer settlement for at least twelve months after the reporting date (terms that could, at the counterparty's option, lead to settlement by issue of equity do not affect classification).

All other liabilities are non-current. The operating cycle is the time between acquiring assets for processing and their realisation in cash; if it cannot be identified, it is assumed to be 12 months. Current maturities of long-term borrowings are shown under short-term borrowings.

lesson.body:
A company may buy back its own shares or other specified securities out of:

- its **free reserves**;
- the **securities premium** account; or
- the **proceeds of any issue** of shares or other specified securities, but **not** proceeds of an earlier issue of the **same kind**.

Main conditions:

- authorised by the articles;
- **special resolution** in general meeting; a buyback of up to **10%** of total paid-up equity capital and free reserves can be approved by a **board resolution**;
- buyback not more than **25%** of the aggregate of paid-up capital and free reserves; for equity shares, not more than 25% of total paid-up equity capital in that financial year;
- post-buyback ratio of secured and unsecured **debt to paid-up capital and free reserves not more than 2:1** (or a higher ratio notified for a class of companies);
- all shares or securities bought back are **fully paid**;
- completed within **one year** of the resolution; no fresh buyback offer within one year of closure of the previous one;
- securities bought back are extinguished and physically destroyed within **7 days** of completion;
- no fresh issue of the same kind of shares for **6 months** (except bonus issue and discharge of existing obligations such as conversion of warrants or ESOPs).
